==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|ōþ-|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|āt-|race, people|lang=ang}}.
Germanic cognates include Old Frisian ''ēþel'', Old High German [[uodil]], Old Norse [[óðal]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈeːðel/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|g=m}}

# ancestral land, [[home]], [[territory]]
#: ''Ic ealne geondhwearf eðel Gotena.''  I travelled through all the country of the Goths.
# the rune '''{{Runr|[[ᛟ]]}}'''

